  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Avinas. Type: Partnership point-trick. Rules: 32 cards. Trumps: QC > 7-Trump > other Qs > Js > Trump-suit A-10-K-9-8. Goal: 61/120 points. Lose = get horns.',
    Player: "Welcome to Avinas! You have 8 cards. Note the Queen of Clubs—it's the highest card in the game. The Seven of the trump suit is the second-highest. Can you work with your partner to reach 61 points and avoid the Horns of the Ram?",
    objective: "Capture at least 61 points in tricks to avoid being 'Horned' (penalized).",
    gameplay: "1. **Determining Trump**: If no 7 was flipped during dealing, the dealer determines trump or it follows a rotation. 2. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. If they cannot, they may trump or discard. 3. **The 'Ram'**: The goal is to reach 61 points. If the declarer's side fails, they receive one 'Horn'. If they fail to get 31 (Schneider), they receive two 'Horns'. 4. **Card Points**: Ace (11), 10 (10), King (4), Queen (3), Jack (2). The Sevens used as trumps count 0 points.",
    keyRules: [
      'Total points in the deck is 120; 60-60 results in a win for the non-bidding side.',
      'The Seven as a high trump is a unique feature that changes the standard Schafkopf strategy.',
      'If a player is dealt two 7s face up during a botched deal, the first one seen usually determines trumps.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
